y-for-ingress?\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2234:   `restore-fn` is called with three arguments, `base entry val`, where\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2238:  [state restore-fn]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2256:          (restore-fn base entry (:value entry)))))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2261:   woke, through `restore-fn` (`base entry val -> state`, the one restore\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2268:  [state restore-fn]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2270:    (or (resume-from-run-queue v' restore-fn) v')))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2302:  [state parked-id resume-val restore-fn]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2306:      (-> (restore-fn new-state parked resume-val)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2475:(defn- gc-roots\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2477:   classifies them (`module/gc-roots`), each entry of `:parked`,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2485:                 (module/gc-roots vm))]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2530:         marked (mark vm snapshot (gc-roots vm extra) (:pinned gc))\n   program        ; last loaded AST program\n   control        ; current AST node or nil\n   env            ; persistent lexical scope map\n   id-counter     ; integer counter for unique IDs\n   parked         ; parked continuations map\n   primitives     ; primitive operations map\n   primitive-profiles ; portable primitive profile projection\n   primitive-canonical-names ; declared aliases for identity reverse lookup\n   modules        ; module registry value\n   make-stream    ; host-supplied stream constructor, or nil\n   call-capacity  ; declared capacity of the FFI pair\n   ready-queue    ; vector of runnable continuations\n   store          ; heap memory map\n   value          ; last computed value\n   wait-set       ; vector of continuations waiting on a transport\n   telemetry      ; telemetry config map ({:stream … :vm-id …}) or nil\n   telemetry-step ; telemetry snapshot counter\n   telemetry-t    ; telemetry transaction counter\n   telemetry-eid  ; telemetry entity-id seed,